The quadratic equation is \(2x^2 - 10x + 5 = 0\).  
Using the quadratic formula \(x = \frac{-B \pm \sqrt{B^2 - 4AC}}{2A}\), where \(A = 2\), \(B = -10\), \(C = 5\):

\[
x = \frac{-(-10) \pm \sqrt{(-10)^2 - 4(2)(5)}}{2(2)}
= \frac{10 \pm \sqrt{100 - 40}}{4}
= \frac{10 \pm \sqrt{60}}{4}
= \frac{10 \pm 2\sqrt{15}}{4}
= \frac{5 \pm \sqrt{15}}{2}.
\]

Thus, the solutions are  
\[
a = \frac{5 + \sqrt{15}}{2}, \quad b = \frac{5 - \sqrt{15}}{2}
\]
(or vice versa).
